From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hexagonrpcd: answer an unsupported call with an error and keep serving

On the OnePlus Pad 4 (SM8850) the ADSP's sensors PD calls apps_std method 36
(sc 0x1f050100) right after INIT_ATTACH_SNS. apps_std implements 32 methods,
so invoke_requested_procedure() logs "Unsupported method: 36 (1f050100)" and
returns 1; run_fastrpc_listener() leaves its loop and hexagonrpcd exits with
status 0. With the upstream unit's Restart=always the service manager starts
it again 3 s later ("restart counter is at 1" on every boot), and the second
instance keeps running.

The error is already in result (AEE_EUNSUPPORTED / AEE_EBADPARM /
AEE_ENOMEMORY): send it back to the DSP for that call, with no output
buffers, and wait for the next call, as for a successful call. The input
buffers of the failed call are freed and the stale output buffer pointer is
dropped (it was freed before the call).

diff --git a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
index 3414974..4aa211f 100644
--- a/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
+++ b/hexagonrpcd/listener.c
@@ -592,8 +592,25 @@ int run_fastrpc_listener(int fd,
 		ret = invoke_requested_procedure(n_ifaces, ifaces,
 						 handle, sc, &result,
 						 decoded, &returned);
-		if (ret)
-			break;
+		if (ret) {
+			/*
+			 * The call cannot be served (an unsupported handle or
+			 * method, missing arguments, no memory): result holds
+			 * the error. Answer the call with it and no output
+			 * buffers, and keep serving. Leaving the loop ends
+			 * hexagonrpcd, and the DSP process loses its file server
+			 * until the service manager starts a new one.
+			 */
+			if (decoded != NULL)
+				iobuf_free(REMOTE_SCALARS_INBUFS(sc), decoded);
+
+			decoded = NULL;
+			returned = NULL;
+			n_outbufs = 0;
+			sc = REMOTE_SCALARS_MAKE(0, 0, 0);
+			ret = 0;
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		if (decoded != NULL)
 			iobuf_free(REMOTE_SCALARS_INBUFS(sc), decoded);
